A||N||2||3fifty||Aux Gauges||||9||
Z||000000||3fifty||05-22-2001||11:16 PM||||I got my wrap around dash from Pisa today. Yep, they sent the wrong dash. How hard is it to add aux gauges to a car that did not come with them? Of course the dash they sent has the big hole that I did not need. Thanks for any input. I hate to go through the ol exchange routine.<P>3fifty one day!!!!!!||||reg||9
Z||000001||Steve Normington||05-23-2001||12:18 AM||||Not too hard. You'll need the aux gage pod shell (the outside of the pod), the gages themselves, wiring pigtail, plexiglass front, trim panel, and the bracked that mounts to the front of the heater/radio pod. You'll need to drill two holes in the metal heater bracked to mount the aux gage bracket (the aux gage bracket can be used as a template) and cut a slot in the dashboard (maybe, depending on your dash) for the wires. Here is the link for the wiring of the gages.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||geyser||05-24-2001||01:47 AM||||That dash is the best addition to my 87 GT. It really makes the car.||||reg||1
